//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 73 - GENUINELY NEW MECHANISM: ICHIMOKU KUMO BREAKOUT WITH CHIKOU (LAGGING SPAN) CONFIRMATION.
//
// The stored scheduled prompt describes a board state ("Attack 37, build its filter stack") more than
// seventy attacks stale. The docs override it, per the prompt's own standing instruction: Attack 37's
// stack was built and closed on cost by Attack 41 back in this lab's early history; the OBV-divergence
// line (Attack 66 + Attack 68's magnitude floor) is the board's current strongest both-halves candidate,
// and its own filter stack closed at two terms after three independent term-3 candidates (Attacks 69,
// 70, 71) each failed a RATCHET v2 clause. Attack 72 (lag-1 return-autocorrelation persistence breakout)
// was that cycle's genuinely-new-mechanism attempt and was DISCARDED (H1 cleared 1.0, H2 reversed to
// 0.857). Attack 72's own queue said the next cycle owed to this board is a further, genuinely new
// mechanism, distinct from every family already tried (VWAP, channel/weekly/range breakouts, liquidity
// sweep, level tap-and-hold, round-number, impulse-bar, session-range, RSI/OBV divergence, order-flow
// absorption, funding-settlement, streak exhaustion, EMA crossover, swing structure breakout, volatility
// shock reversal, autocorrelation regime). This build is that instruction, continuing numbering after
// Attack 72, not Attack 37.
//
// ==================== THE CLAIM, ARGUED FROM THE MECHANISM (LESSON 15/17: BEFORE running, not after) ==
// Every breakout mechanism tried on this board so far (33, 34/35, 36, 46, 50, 57/58, 59/63) defines its
// level from a RAW price extreme (a rolling high/low, a calendar high/low, a session high/low) or from a
// fast/slow moving-average cross. The Ichimoku Kumo (cloud) is a different kind of level entirely: its
// two edges (Senkou Span A and B) are each built from AVERAGES OF RANGE EXTREMES at two different
// lookbacks (9/26-bar midpoint and 52-bar midpoint) and then displaced FORWARD in time by 26 bars, so the
// cloud a bar sits inside today was computed from price action a full 26 bars before "now" arrived at
// that computation. That displacement is the mechanism's actual claim: a support/resistance zone built
// from where the market's own consensus range sat a lag ago is a different (and slower-moving,
// consensus-weighted) object than any raw N-bar extreme this board has tested, and price decisively
// clearing it should mean something a same-bar extreme cannot capture. The Chikou (lagging) span adds an
// orthogonal confirmation: today's close compared against the close price from 26 bars ago (the price
// level the Chikou line is plotted against) checks whether the move is unobstructed relative to where
// price actually was a lag ago, not merely relative to the cloud's own construction.
//
// Mechanism (LONG ONLY, bare, no filter stack): tenkan = (highest(high,9)+lowest(low,9))/2. kijun =
// (highest(high,26)+lowest(low,26))/2. senkouA_raw = (tenkan+kijun)/2. senkouB_raw =
// (highest(high,52)+lowest(low,52))/2. The cloud IN EFFECT at the current bar is senkouA_raw and
// senkouB_raw as they stood 26 bars ago (senkouA_raw[26], senkouB_raw[26]) -- this is the standard
// Ichimoku forward-displacement read backward, using only the `[]` history operator, no
// request.security, no arrays. cloudTop = max of the two; cloudBottom = min of the two. Entry trigger:
// close crosses over cloudTop (ta.crossover). Chikou confirmation: close > close[26] (today's close
// stands above the close price 26 bars back -- the price the lagging span is compared against). Long
// entry: breakoutTrigger AND chikouOk AND R-floor (LESSON 3, by exclusion). Stop at cloudBottom -- the
// OPPOSITE edge of the same cloud the entry broke out of, a genuinely different object from cloudTop
// (LESSON 5: entry level and stop level are never the same object). Target fixed at 2R (lab convention;
// HARD LESSON 13 found the R:R axis neutral, so no tuning credit spent hunting "the best" multiple).
// Flip/regime response (STANDING REQUIREMENT item 3): a bearish flip is close crossing back under
// cloudBottom -- because the entry condition itself requires a FRESH crossover of cloudTop, price cannot
// re-trigger a new long without first reclaiming the cloud top again, so the stand-down is structural to
// the trigger definition, not a separate bolted-on counter. Existing open trades still resolve on their
// own fixed SL/TP, unchanged by a mid-trade flip (no custom var-trail, no signal-based early exit).
//
// AUDIT, one line per leg:
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) - EXCLUSION via rBig on rLong = close - cloudBottom (the entry/stop distance at
//        the breakout bar), never clamped: a trade needing a floor-widened stop is skipped, not taken
//        with an artificially enlarged risk.
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) - slPx = cloudBottom, the far edge of the same Kumo the breakout
//        cleared -- a distinct object from cloudTop (the entry/trigger level), never a tick beyond the
//        signal price itself.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) - LONG ONLY this cycle, following this lab's own established
//        convention for a first pass on a new mechanism (Attacks 59/63/65/66/72 all opened long- or
//        short-only and reported the other side as a standing asymmetry); the short side (a bearish Kumo
//        breakdown with its own geometry, never mirrored) is deferred and reported as outstanding.
//   BINDING (E17) - breakoutTrigger AND chikouOk AND rBig must all independently bind; this is the FIRST
//        run of this mechanism, and per Attack 72's own precedent only two credits are budgeted this
//        cycle for the H1/H2 pair, so no per-term counter build was affordable -- the realized trade
//        count against the pre-run frequency estimate below is the binding evidence this cycle can
//        afford, and a per-term counter build is queued if this clears the kill rule.
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) - cloudTop/cloudBottom encode a PRICE-RANGE CONSENSUS statistic (averaged range
//        extremes at three different lookbacks, time-displaced); chikouOk reads a RAW CLOSE-TO-CLOSE
//        comparison across time with no range component at all; rBig/slPx read a PRICE DISTANCE from
//        entry to the cloud's far edge. Three independent quantities, no other term in this build repeats
//        any of them.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8, fourth-confirmation check) - breakoutTrigger is a crossing/transition
//        event (ta.crossover); chikouOk is a SINGLE-BAR point comparison (close vs. close[26] evaluated
//        on the same bar as the trigger), not a filter phrased as "already been true for N bars" the way
//        the coil/thrust, zone-tap/engulf and EMA-crossover/rising failures were -- so there is no
//        arm-then-expire timing mismatch for this pair to fall into. Checked explicitly against the
//        generalized rule and it does not apply here.
//   CASCADE (HARD LESSON 42/43) - LONG at 100% equity, single entry id "L", pyramiding=1; expect
//        cascadeRatio 1 / maxCascadeDepth 1 on both halves, confirmed below.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale, no custom var-trail.
//
// FREQUENCY ESTIMATE, REGISTERED BEFORE RUNNING (HARD LESSON 4: a hypothesis to score, not a fact):
//   cloudTop is itself a smoothed, time-displaced level (built from 9/26/52-bar range midpoints), slower
//   moving than a raw N-bar extreme but still crossed by volatile 15m BTC price often. No directly
//   comparable prior measurement exists on this board for a cloud-edge cross specifically; anchoring
//   loosely on the VWAP-cross flip frequency (007's family) and the EMA-crossover order of magnitude
//   (Attack 57's raw 2154 crosses before filtering) as bounds either side of this level's smoothness,
//   pre-registering 200-700 trades per half, to be scored against the actual count in either direction.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17), READ PER THE PROMPT'S OWN KILL RULE:
//   * H1 (never-tuned, 2022-01-01 to 2024-06-08) PROFIT FACTOR BELOW 1.0 -> DISCARD immediately. Do not
//     run H2. Do not add filters to rescue H1.
//   * H1 clears 1.0 -> run H2 (2024-06-08 to 2026-09-01) as the second and last credit this cycle.
//   * BOTH halves clear 1.0 -> a genuine both-halves candidate, joining Attack 37/46/66-68 on the board;
//     report avg loser, win rate and max DD alongside PF (the board's three-drawdown-category taxonomy),
//     and queue it for a filter stack exactly as Attack 37/66 earned theirs.
//   * H1 clears but H2 does not -> report both, DISCARD as a candidate (per Attack 53/72's precedent),
//     not as evidence the whole family is dead.
//   REPORT GROSS, COMMISSION, ACHIEVED WIN/LOSS RATIO, AVG LOSER AND WIN RATE alongside net, on whichever
//     half(s) actually run.

strategy("BTC Attack73 Ichimoku Kumo+Chikou breakout", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

tenkanLen   = input.int(9, "Tenkan lookback")
kijunLen    = input.int(26, "Kijun lookback")
senkouBLen  = input.int(52, "Senkou B lookback")
cloudShift  = input.int(26, "Cloud/Chikou displacement (bars)")
minRpct     = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3)")
targetR     = input.float(2.0, "Target, multiple of R (lab convention)")
maxBars     = input.int(192, "Max bars in trade")

tenkan = (ta.highest(high, tenkanLen) + ta.lowest(low, tenkanLen)) / 2
kijun  = (ta.highest(high, kijunLen) + ta.lowest(low, kijunLen)) / 2
senkouA_raw = (tenkan + kijun) / 2
senkouB_raw = (ta.highest(high, senkouBLen) + ta.lowest(low, senkouBLen)) / 2

cloudA = senkouA_raw[cloudShift]
cloudB = senkouB_raw[cloudShift]
cloudTop    = math.max(cloudA, cloudB)
cloudBottom = math.min(cloudA, cloudB)

cloudReady = not na(cloudTop) and not na(cloudBottom)

breakoutTrigger = cloudReady and ta.crossover(close, cloudTop)
chikouOk = not na(close[cloudShift]) and close > close[cloudShift]

rLong = cloudReady ? close - cloudBottom : na
minR  = close * minRpct / 100
rBig  = not na(rLong) and rLong >= minR

goLong = breakoutTrigger and chikouOk and rBig

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := cloudBottom
    tpPx   := close + targetR * rLong
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(cloudTop, title="CloudTop")
plot(cloudBottom, title="CloudBottom")
plot(chikouOk ? 1 : 0, title="ChikouOk")
